---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import type { CasePart } from "../types";
import setup from "./emotion-paired-setup.png";

interface Props {
  part: CasePart;
}
const { part } = Astro.props;
const imageWidths = [360, 540, 704].filter((width) => width <= setup.width);
const cells = Array.from({ length: 100 });
---

{part === "intro" && (
  <p>
    I contributed across the behavioral and fNIRS data-analysis workflow,
    including preprocessing, activation analysis, interbrain synchrony and
    multivariate pattern analysis.
  </p>
)}

{part === "visual" && (
  <figure class="portfolio-figure emotion-setup">
    <Image
      src={setup}
      format="webp"
      widths={imageWidths}
      sizes="(min-width: 752px) 704px, calc(100vw - 48px)"
      width={setup.width}
      height={setup.height}
      alt="Two participants wearing fNIRS caps sit across from one another with computer displays between them."
      loading="eager"
      fetchpriority="high"
      decoding="async"
    />
    <figcaption>
      Paired fNIRS recording during face-to-face interaction (Figure 1B, Yang et
      al., 2026). fNIRS tracks changes in blood oxygenation over the sampled
      cortical regions.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
)}

{part === "body" && (
  <>
    <h2>From interaction to analysis</h2>
    <p>
      Participants viewed and rated an image, completed a regulation
      interaction, then viewed and rated the same image again. One person, the
      regulator, offered reappraisal or a distraction task; the other, the
      target, responded.
    </p>
    <figure class="portfolio-figure emotion-analysis">
      <div
        class="portfolio-diagram emotion-map"
        aria-label="Task and analysis workflow"
      >
        <section class="emotion-task" aria-labelledby="emotion-task-title">
          <h3 id="emotion-task-title">Two people, one interaction</h3>
          <ol>
            <li>View image and rate</li>
            <li>Regulation interaction</li>
            <li>View the same image again and rate</li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <div class="emotion-data-streams">
          <section
            class="emotion-ratings emotion-lane"
            aria-labelledby="emotion-ratings-title"
          >
            <h3 id="emotion-ratings-title">Ratings</h3>
            <p>Compare pre/post ratings across strategy and role.</p>
            <p class="emotion-small">Account for dyads.</p>
          </section>
          <section
            class="emotion-fnirs emotion-lane"
            aria-labelledby="emotion-fnirs-title"
          >
            <h3 id="emotion-fnirs-title">Simultaneous fNIRS</h3>
            <ol class="emotion-preprocessing">
              <li>Quality checks and preprocessing</li>
              <li>Hemoglobin time series</li>
            </ol>
            <p class="emotion-split-label">Separate analysis branches</p>
            <div class="emotion-neural-branches">
              <section
                class="emotion-branch"
                aria-labelledby="emotion-activation-title"
              >
                <h4 id="emotion-activation-title">Activation</h4>
                <p>GLM: task-related HbO estimates</p>
                <p class="emotion-small">Compare strategy and role.</p>
              </section>
              <section
                class="emotion-branch"
                aria-labelledby="emotion-synchrony-title"
              >
                <h4 id="emotion-synchrony-title">Interbrain synchrony</h4>
                <p>
                  Correlate the two participants’ regional signals within each
                  trial.
                </p>
                <div class="emotion-matrix-block">
                  <p class="emotion-matrix-title">Schematic feature matrix</p>
                  <div class="emotion-matrix-layout">
                    <span class="emotion-column-label">
                      Target ROIs (columns)
                    </span>
                    <span class="emotion-row-label">Regulator ROIs (rows)</span>
                    <div class="emotion-matrix" aria-hidden="true">
                      {cells.map((_, index) => (
                        <span class:list={{ "selected-pair": index === 36 }} />
                      ))}
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <p class="emotion-small">
                    Ten regions per person. Each cell represents a correlation
                    between two regions; one pair is outlined.
                  </p>
                </div>
                <p class="emotion-feature-label">
                  Matrix values supply <strong>features</strong> for
                  classification.
                </p>
              </section>
            </div>
          </section>
        </div>

        <section
          class="emotion-classification"
          aria-labelledby="emotion-classification-title"
        >
          <h3 id="emotion-classification-title">Multivariate classification</h3>
          <div class="emotion-inputs">
            <p>
              <strong>Features:</strong> interbrain-synchrony matrix.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>Target labels:</strong> assigned strategy and each
              person’s rating-defined success.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="emotion-targets">
            <div>
              <h4>Which strategy?</h4>
              <p>Reappraisal or distraction</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h4>Regulation success?</h4>
              <ul>
                <li>Regulator success</li>
                <li>Target success</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="emotion-small">
            Success meant a more positive rating when viewing the same image
            again. Classification addressed three targets and was evaluated
            using within-participant cross-validation.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        Simplified analysis workflow from the published study. The matrix
        illustrates feature construction.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p>
      Behavioral models compared ratings before and after regulation across
      strategies and roles. Activation analysis estimated task-related changes
      in oxygenated hemoglobin and compared responses across strategies and
      roles.
    </p>
    <p>
      For each trial, correlations between the two participants’ regional
      signals formed an interbrain-synchrony matrix. These cross-person patterns
      provided features for multivariate classification.
    </p>
    <h2>Accounting for interacting pairs</h2>
    <p>
      Behavioral and activation models accounted for shared variation within
      each dyad through a dyad random intercept. This retained the paired
      structure when comparing strategies and roles.
    </p>
    <h2>Published findings</h2>
    <p>
      The published analyses found role- and strategy-dependent neural
      responses, alongside interbrain patterns informative about regulation
      strategy and success.
    </p>
    <details class="portfolio-methods">
      <summary>Analysis details</summary>
      <p>
        Each trial produced a 10×10 matrix of Pearson correlations between the
        two participants’ regional time series. SVM-based classification
        evaluated strategy and role-specific success using five-fold
        cross-validation within participants. Preprocessing included
        signal-quality checks, motion-artifact handling and conversion from
        optical measurements to hemoglobin changes.
      </p>
    </details>
    <h2>Publication</h2>
    <p class="emotion-citation">
      Yang, Y., He, J., Wang, L., Wang, J., Xu, J., Jiang, X., Ao, N., Zhang,
      P., Chen, Y., Wang, M., &amp; Du, F. (2026). Bidirectional Benefits:
      Interbrain Synchronization and Role-Specific Neural Signatures in
      Interpersonal Emotion Regulation. <em>Emotion.</em>
    </p>
  </>
)}

<style>
  .emotion-setup {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
  .emotion-setup img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 0.85rem;
  }
  .emotion-analysis {
    margin-block: 1.75rem;
  }
  .emotion-map {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 1.5rem);
    color: var(--portfolio-ink);
    background: var(--portfolio-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--portfolio-line);
    border-radius: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .emotion-map h3,
  .emotion-map h4 {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    font-family: inherit;
    color: var(--portfolio-ink);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }
  .emotion-map h4 {
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
  .emotion-map p {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
    color: inherit;
    line-height: inherit;
  }
  .emotion-map ol,
  .emotion-map ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }
  .emotion-map li {
    padding-left: 0.15rem;
    margin: 0.3rem 0 0;
    color: inherit;
  }
  .emotion-task ol {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0.6rem 1.7rem;
    margin-top: 0.8rem;
  }
  .emotion-task li {
    padding-right: 0.25rem;
  }
  .emotion-data-streams {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    border-block: 1px solid var(--portfolio-line);
    padding-block: 1.25rem;
  }
  .emotion-lane {
    min-width: 0;
    padding-left: 1rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--portfolio-line);
  }
  .emotion-fnirs {
    border-color: var(--portfolio-accent);
  }
  .emotion-preprocessing {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.15rem;
  }
  .emotion-map .emotion-split-label {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--portfolio-muted);
  }
  .emotion-neural-branches {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.75fr) minmax(0, 1.25fr);
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .emotion-branch {
    min-width: 0;
    padding-top: 0.75rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--portfolio-line);
  }
  .emotion-map .emotion-small {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--portfolio-muted);
  }
  .emotion-matrix-block {
    margin-top: 0.9rem;
  }
  .emotion-map .emotion-matrix-title {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .emotion-matrix-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 4.5rem) minmax(0, 9rem);
    grid-template-rows: auto auto;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 14rem;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    align-items: center;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--portfolio-muted);
  }
  .emotion-column-label {
    grid-column: 2;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .emotion-row-label {
    grid-column: 1;
    grid-row: 2;
  }
  .emotion-matrix {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(10, minmax(0, 1fr));
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    grid-column: 2;
    grid-row: 2;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--portfolio-line);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--portfolio-line);
  }
  .emotion-matrix span {
    border-right: 1px solid var(--portfolio-line);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--portfolio-line);
  }
  .emotion-matrix .selected-pair {
    outline: 2px solid var(--portfolio-accent);
    outline-offset: -2px;
  }
  .emotion-map .emotion-feature-label {
    margin-top: 0.9rem;
  }
  .emotion-classification {
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .emotion-targets {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  .emotion-targets > div {
    padding: 0.8rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--portfolio-line);
    border-radius: 0.6rem;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .emotion-citation {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  @media (max-width: 35rem) {
    .emotion-task ol,
    .emotion-neural-branches,
    .emotion-targets {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
    .emotion-task ol {
      gap: 0.35rem;
    }
    .emotion-task ol {
      padding-left: 20px;
    }
    .emotion-map .emotion-preprocessing {
      list-style-position: inside;
      padding-left: 0;
    }
    .emotion-map .emotion-preprocessing li {
      padding-left: 0;
    }
    .emotion-map {
      padding: 12px;
      font-size: 0.9375rem;
    }
    .emotion-lane {
      padding-left: 10px;
    }
    .emotion-targets > div {
      padding: 12px;
    }
    .emotion-matrix-layout {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      grid-template-rows: auto auto auto;
      max-width: 180px;
      gap: 8px;
    }
    .emotion-column-label {
      grid-column: 1;
      grid-row: 1;
      text-align: left;
    }
    .emotion-row-label {
      grid-column: 1;
      grid-row: 3;
    }
    .emotion-matrix {
      grid-column: 1;
      grid-row: 2;
      width: min(100%, 160px);
    }
  }
</style>
